<div class="card">
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>How many pounds in a kilogram?</h3>
    <p>1 kilogram is equal to <strong>2.2046 pounds</strong>. This is the international standard conversion factor.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>How do I convert kg to lbs manually?</h3>
    <p>Multiply the number of kilograms by <strong>2.2046</strong>. For example: <code>50 kg × 2.2046 = 110.23 lbs</code>. Or just use our converter above.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Why is 1 kg = 2.2046 lbs?</h3>
    <p>The pound is legally defined as exactly 0.45359237 kg. So 1 kg = 1 / 0.45359237 = 2.20462262185 lbs.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Is this converter free?</h3>
    <p>Yes, 100% free. No sign-up, no limits, no hidden fees.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-item">
    <h3>Which countries use kg vs lbs?</h3>
    <p>Most countries use kilograms (metric system). Pounds are mainly used in the <strong>United States</strong>, and for body weight measurement in the UK and Canada.</p>
  </div>
</div>
